.TH GENESIS-RETINA 1 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-retina \- legacy name for the retired standalone retina process
.SH STATUS
.B genesis-retina
is not a current executable and must not be launched. The former
standalone V4L2 capture process and its
.I /genesis_retina
shared-memory contract have been retired. Current visual capture is
a daemon-owned optic-capture limb using the canonical
.I /genesis_optic_nerve
mapping.
.PP
On Linux, the daemon opens the V4L2 device named by
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
(default
.IR /dev/video0 ).
On Android, the Camera2 foreground adapter forwards frames to the
daemon over loopback. Both platforms publish into the same optic
frame contract; the mind reads it through the existing perception
path.
.PP
This compatibility manual is retained so old references resolve.
For current architecture, frame formats, camera controls, optical
processing, illumination adaptation, phototransduction, and face
recognition, read
.BR genesis-vision (7).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesis (1),
.BR genesis-cli (1),
.BR genesis-daemon (8),
.BR genesis-vision (7)
